{'symbol': 'TXT', 'date': '2020-07-30 11:30:00', 'title': 'TEXTRON CEO EXPECTS 2020 AVIATION DELIVERIES TO BE DOWN 30% TO 40% - CONF CALL', 'text': 'TEXTRON CEO SAYS AIRCRAFT AFTERMARKET SALES ARE OFF LOWS HIT IN APRIL - CONF CALL.TEXTRON CFO SAYS FALL IN CITATION JET VOLUME IN Q2 MAINLY REFLECTED A DECLINE IN DEMAND RELATED TO THE PANDEMIC, AND DELAYS IN THE AIRCRAFT ACCEPTANCE RELATED TO COVID-19 TRAVEL RESTRICTIONS.TEXTRON CEO SAYS AVIATION SALES TEAM IS BACK IN THE FIELD AND EXPECTS TO SEE HIGHER NEW JET DELIVERIES IN H2 ON SEQUENTIAL BASIS.TEXTRON CEO SAYS SEEING ACTIVITY ON TURBOPROPS AND THE LIGHT JET SIDE.TEXTRON CEO NOT SEEING AS MUCH ACTIVITY YET IN TERMS OF LATITUDE AND LONGITUDE JET SALES, BUT HAVE DIALOGUE GOING ON WITH CUSTOMERS.TEXTRON CEO SAYS THERE IS DEMAND OUT THERE AS CUSTOMERS ARE LOOKING AT INCREASED USE OF PRIVATE AVIATION; THIS IS A HEALTHY THING IN THE MID TO LONG TERM.TEXTRON CEO SAYS EXPECTS TO SEE JET ORDER ACTIVITY PICK UP STARTING 2021.TEXTRON CEO SAYS CORPORATE CUSTOMERS ARE WATCHING THEIR CAPEX CLOSELY; PACE OF ECONOMIC RECOVERY WILL DRIVE ORDERS FOR CO.TEXTRON CFO SAYS EXPECTS TO BE CASH FLOW POSITIVE IN H2 2020 AND THE FULL YEAR.TEXTRON CEO SAYS EXPECTS CORPORATE AMERICA TO START MAKING CAPEX COMMITMENTS AGAIN BEGINNING 2021.TEXTRON CEO SAYS EXPECTS TO SEE BACKLOG FOR LARGER AIRCRAFT FROM NETJETS PICK UP IN THIRD AND FOURTH QUARTER.TEXTRON CEO SAYS EXPECT AVIATION DELIVERIES TO BE DOWN BETWEEN 30% AND 40% IN 2020.TEXTRON CFO SAYS THERE WAS NO CHANGE IN THE NETJET BACKLOG IN Q2.'}{'symbol': 'TXT', 'date': '2020-07-30 09:30:00', 'title': 'TEXTRON REPORTS Q2 ADJUSTED NON-GAAP EARNINGS PER SHARE $0.13', 'text': 'TEXTRON REPORTS SECOND QUARTER 2020 RESULTS.Q2 ADJUSTED NON-GAAP EARNINGS PER SHARE $0.13.Q2 LOSS PER SHARE $0.40.Q2 EARNINGS PER SHARE ESTIMATE $-0.08 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.QTRLY REVENUES AT TEXTRON AVIATION OF $747 MILLION WERE DOWN $376 MILLION FROM Q2 OF 2019.TEXTRON AVIATION BACKLOG AT END OF Q2 WAS $1.4 BILLION.BELL BACKL